# nosemgrep: package_managers.npm.npm-missing-minimum-release-age.npm-missing-minimum-release-age
# (min-release-age is an npm 11.10 setting; this repo installs with pnpm 9, which
# does not read it. Release-age gating is Renovate's minimumReleaseAge: 7 days and
# installs run with --frozen-lockfile, so nothing new resolves outside a reviewed PR.)
# The contract package (@datagriff/todo-api-contract) lives on GitHub Packages.
# Only the scope -> registry mapping is committed. Auth comes from outside the
# repo: CI writes an _authToken line from NODE_AUTH_TOKEN (see the workflows);
# locally `task registry:login` writes one to your user-level ~/.npmrc from your
# gh login (or add `//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=<PAT with read:packages>`
# there yourself), or use `task contract:link` against a sibling checkout of
# aws.contract.template while developing both.
@datagriff:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
